    "notation_and_period": {
      "id": "notation_and_period",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The repeating block is also called the period. Count the digits in that block, not the total digits shown in a calculator approximation. For example, 0.(27) repeats the two-digit block 27; it is not the same as 0.2(7), where only 7 repeats after a non-repeating 2.\n\nNotation prevents ambiguity. When reading the repeat notation, say the non-repeating prefix first, then name the full block that repeats. This will later tell you how many 9s and zeroes belong in the denominator.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_notation_and_period"
        }
      ]
    },
