    "multi_digit_mixed_period": {
      "id": "multi_digit_mixed_period",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "When the repeating block has more than one digit, use one 9 for each repeating digit, then append zeroes for the prefix length. For 0.2(35), the prefix is 2 and the period is 35. The numerator is 235 − 2 = 233; the denominator is 990. Therefore 0.2(35) = 233/990.\n\nThis rule comes from shifting until the repeating tails line up: 100x − 10x cancels the common tail. It is not a rule to put every displayed digit over a power of ten; that would represent a terminating approximation instead of the exact recurring value.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_multi_digit_mixed_period"
        }
      ]
